Reason:
The patch changes `l2cap_register_user()` and `l2cap_unregister_user()` to use `mutex_lock(&conn->lock)` and `mutex_unlock(&conn->lock)`, the same lock that `l2cap_conn_del()` uses to protect `conn->users` and `conn->hchan`. By applying consistent locking, all accesses to these fields are properly synchronized, eliminating the race condition that could cause use-after-free and list corruption.

